---
import ContentLayout from '../layouts/ContentLayout.astro';

const asideLinks = [
  { label: 'Current status', href: '#current-status' },
  { label: 'If links are added', href: '#if-links-are-added' },
  { label: 'Editorial independence', href: '#editorial-independence' },
  { label: 'Questions', href: '#questions' },
];
---

<ContentLayout
  title="Affiliate disclosure"
  metaTitle="Affiliate Disclosure: Current Status"
  description="FixProblemNow currently has no affiliate links, sponsored placements or advertising. Read how any future commercial links would be disclosed."
  canonical="/affiliate-disclosure/"
  eyebrow="Disclosure"
  intro="This page records the site’s current commercial relationships and how any future affiliate link or sponsored placement would be disclosed."
  updated="2026-11-15"
  asideLinks={asideLinks}
  asideNote="No affiliate link is currently used anywhere on the site."
>
  <h2 id="current-status">Current status</h2>
  <p>
    At the time of publication, FixProblemNow contains no affiliate links, no sponsored content, no
    paid product placements, and no display advertising. The site does not earn a commission when
    you click a link to a manufacturer, retailer, or repair service.
  </p>
  <p>
    Links to manufacturer support pages and official documentation are provided because they are
    the authoritative source for a tool, download, or procedure. They are not commercial links.
  </p>

  <h2 id="if-links-are-added">If links are added</h2>
  <p>
    If the site later uses affiliate links, the following rules will apply:
  </p>
  <ul class="checklist">
    <li>A clear disclosure will appear on the page, before the first affiliate link, not only in the footer.</li>
    <li>The disclosure will say that the site may earn a commission and that the price to you is unchanged.</li>
    <li>Sponsored content will be labelled as sponsored, and the sponsor will not control the troubleshooting steps.</li>
    <li>Affiliate status will not determine which product is recommended or how a guide is ranked.</li>
    <li>This page will be updated with the date and the categories of links in use.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="editorial-independence">Editorial independence</h2>
  <p>
    Commercial relationships do not purchase a favourable conclusion, a removed safety warning, or a
    higher position in search results. The <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> explains
    how sources and safety are handled. If a guide recommends a manufacturer’s own tool, that is
    because the manufacturer controls the download or recovery process, not because of a payment.
  </p>

  <h2 id="questions">Questions</h2>
  <p>
    If you see a link that looks commercial but is not disclosed, report it through the
    <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> and choose the general feedback topic. The page will be
    reviewed and the disclosure corrected if needed.
  </p>
</ContentLayout>
